## Part 3: Combined Use

If you use this project in its entirety (both code and data):

- The **code** is available under the MIT License (permissive, commercial use allowed)
- The **data** remains subject to the restrictions above (non-commercial for CC BY-NC-ND portions)
- Your overall usage rights are limited by the most restrictive license component (the data)

**Practical Implications:**
- ✅ **Open Source Projects:** Fully compatible (non-commercial)
- ✅ **Research & Education:** Fully compatible
- ⚠️ **Commercial Products:** Code is freely usable (MIT), but data requires permission from original authors
- ⚠️ **SaaS Applications:** Requires permission if monetized; free for non-commercial services

